Consider the function given by N(x) = x/||x|| where x is a vector in R³. 
Note that N is not defined if x = 0, so the largest possible domain for N is R³ - {0}. 
The range of N consists of all unit vectors in R³. 
The function N is the "normalization function" that is, the function that takes a nonzero vector in R³ and returns the unit vector that points in the same direction. 

